column2:
That was the first part of our journey. 

Now accompany me safely to {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column3:
Det var foerste del af vores rejse.

Ledsag mig nu sikkert til {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column2:
Enough of these stressful deals.

In the hope that I have not overtaxed your patience please now take me to {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column3:
Nok af disse anstrengende handler.

I haabet om ikke at have sat jeres taalmodighed for haardt paa proeve, bring mig nu til {%t:0D}.

{%V:06} {%N:07}

column2:
{%V:0E} {%N:0F},

The map was divided into nine pieces among the crew and we spread out in all directions of the compass. No idea where the other pieces are, but I'll keep my ears open.

{%V:0C} {%N:0D}

column3:
{%V:0E} {%N:0F},

Kortet blev delt i ni stykker blandt besaetningen, og vi spredtes for alle vinde. Ingen anelse om, hvor de andre stykker er, men jeg holder oererne aabne.

{%V:0C} {%N:0D}

column2:
You have fulfilled the mission and shall receive the reward as agreed!

Thank you very much!

{%V:0A} {%N:0C}

column3:
I har fuldfoert opgaven og skal have den aftalte beloenning!

Mange tak!

{%V:0A} {%N:0C}

column2:
Dear {%5:00}{%N:07},

News of the successes of our tranquil town has spread far beyond the town's borders. Now evil powers, full of malice, are planning to rob us of our best by demanding a contribution of the fruit of our hard labour. It has been reported to us that a large army of mercenaries is on its way, and that these fiends will overrun us, murdering, plundering, and burning.Let us take precautionary measures to protect our homes, since we can no longer turn back the bloody storm.

The Town {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Kaere {%5:00}{%N:07},

Rygtet om vores fredelige bys fremgang har bredt sig langt ud over byens graenser. Nu planlaegger onde magter, fulde af ondskab, at beroeve os det bedste ved at kraeve en del af frugten af vores haarde arbejde. Det er meldt os, at en stor haer af lejesoldater er paa vej, og at disse djaevle vil overrende os, myrdende, plyndrende og braendende. Lad os tage forholdsregler for at beskytte vores hjem, for den blodige storm kan vi ikke laengere afvende.

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Citizens of  {%t:04}!

Hordes of marauding foreign troops are sweeping through towns, robbing and murdering without mercy. There is no limit to their atrocities. Whether our prayers - that they might refrain from coming to our beautiful town - have been heard, is yet uncertain.
Arm yourselves, reinforce the walls, and stand bravely with your arms!May the walls hold as steadfastly as our courage!

The Town {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Borgere i {%t:04}!

Horder af plyndrende fremmede tropper drager gennem byerne, roever og myrder uden naade. Der er ingen graense for deres grusomheder. Om vores boenner - at de maa skaane vores smukke by - er blevet hoert, er endnu uvist.
Bevaebn jer, forstaerk murene og staa modigt med vaaben i haand! Maatte murene staa lige saa fast som vores mod!

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Dear Sir,

On their last shore leave, the crew was sitting in a tavern as usual when a drunken sailor bawled out stories about the ship's kobold through the room. He talked about his last ship that was taken by the ship's kobold, and that he was the only one to escape. You know, I do not pay a lot of attention to this superstition but the crew has been a little restless since then. I have got the situation under control and merely wanted to submit a report. 

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Paa deres seneste landlov sad besaetningen som saedvanlig paa en kro, da en fuld soemand broelede historier om skibsnissen ud i lokalet. Han fortalte om sit seneste skib, som skibsnissen havde taget, og at han var den eneste, der slap vaek. I ved, at jeg ikke giver meget for denne overtro, men besaetningen har vaeret lidt urolig siden. Jeg har situationen under kontrol og ville blot aflaegge rapport.

Styrmanden paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

These credulous scary-cats have again picked up something about the ship's kobold. This invisible spirit supposedly protects each and every ship, and that should it leave the ship, it would go down with crew and cargo. You know the legend that a ship's kobold shows himself before he leaves a ship. However, these credible sailors now see him grinning from behind every plank. The morale is not very good, that's why you should see about it yourself!

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Disse godtroende kujoner har igen opsnappet noget om skibsnissen. Denne usynlige aand skulle beskytte hvert eneste skib, og forlod den skibet, ville det gaa ned med mand og last. I kender sagnet om, at skibsnissen viser sig, foer den forlader et skib. Men nu ser disse godtroende soemaend den grine bag hver planke. Moralen er ikke for god, derfor boer I selv se paa sagen!

Styrmanden paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

This cowardly pack has fled. Here in {%t:08} many sailors have discharged, except for a few courageous ones, due to fear of the ship's kobold. For better or for worse, you will have to engage a new crew before you can set sail again.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Dette feje pak er flygtet. Her i {%t:08} er mange matroser afmoenstret af frygt for skibsnissen, paa naer nogle faa modige. Hvad enten I vil eller ej, maa I hyre en ny besaetning, foer vi kan saette sejl igen.

Styrmanden paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

There is talk of unusual sightings near the town of {%t:08}. Several sailors, independent of each other, are said to have seen a ghost ship gliding across the sea and this, despite a calm wind. The crew's heart dropped to the sole of their feet, but they are bravely carrying out their duties. I have doubled the guard to keep things quiet.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Der tales om usaedvanlige syner naer {%t:08}. Flere soemaend har, uafhaengigt af hinanden, set et spoegelsesskib glide hen over havet, og det i vindstille. Besaetningen fik hjertet op i halsen, men de passer tappert deres tjeneste. Jeg har fordoblet vagten for at holde roen.

Styrmanden paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

The fairy tale of the ship's kobold is again doing the rounds among the crew. I have heard of cases where the crew worked itself into such a state, that the whole ship was put in danger. I will be harder on the sailors than normal so that they get rid of this dangerous superstition from their heads as soon as possible.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Eventyret om skibsnissen gaar igen blandt besaetningen. Jeg har hoert om tilfaelde, hvor besaetningen ophidsede sig saa meget, at hele skibet kom i fare. Jeg vil vaere haardere ved matroserne end normalt, saa de snarest faar denne farlige overtro ud af hovedet.

Styrmanden paa {%s:09}

column2:
Dear Sir,

Some of the older sailors are telling the younger ones, that the ship's kobold leaves all ships whose shipping line does not deal in a god fearing way. I was able to put aside the on setting restlessness among the crew, by telling them that you are the most honest trader in the entire Hanse. Everyone is now concentrating on their work on board.

Steersman of the {%s:09}

column3:
Herre,

Nogle af de aeldre soemaend fortaeller de yngre, at skibsnissen forlader alle skibe, hvis reder ikke handler gudfrygtigt. Jeg kunne daempe den begyndende uro blandt besaetningen ved at sige, at I er den aerligste handelsmand i hele Hansaen. Alle passer nu deres arbejde om bord.

Styrmanden paa {%s:09}

column2:
{%7:00},

The passenger that we took on board in {%t:01} and were supposed to be taking to {%t:0A} has disappeared! I've had the crew scour the ship from the keel to the crow's nest, but there was no trace of him to be found anywhere.

Helmsman of the {%s:06}

column3:
{%7:00},

Passageren, som vi tog om bord i {%t:01} og skulle bringe til {%t:0A}, er forsvundet! Jeg har ladet besaetningen gennemsoege skibet fra koelen til udkigstoenden, men der var ikke spor af ham nogen steder.

Styrmanden paa {%s:06}

column2:
{%7:00}{%N:07},

Thank you for your help. Please obtain the following goods for me and get them to {%t:05}, in good condition and within 20 days:

{%B:09}{%w:10}
{%B:0A}{%w:11}
{%B:0B}{%w:12}
{%B:0C}{%w:13}
{%B:0D}{%w:14}
{%B:0E}{%w:15}

Store the goods there, in your trading office. I will have them collected at the given time.

{%V:16} {%N:06}

column3:
{%7:00}{%N:07},

Tak for jeres hjaelp. Skaf mig venligst foelgende varer og bring dem til {%t:05} i god stand og inden 20 dage:

{%B:09}{%w:10}
{%B:0A}{%w:11}
{%B:0B}{%w:12}
{%B:0C}{%w:13}
{%B:0D}{%w:14}
{%B:0E}{%w:15}

Oplagr varerne der, i jeres kontor. Jeg lader dem hente paa det fastsatte tidspunkt.

{%V:16} {%N:06}

column2:
Estate of Mr Jakob Blank

Last night, Mr Jakob Blank died of natural causes in his {%t:09} home. He does not leave any descendants, and his recently amended will and testament names the {%R:00} Leopold Jantzen as his sole heir. An examination of his estate reveals that Jakob Blank, who ended his days living in impoverished circumstances, had a promissory note in the amount of 500,000\C.
The full amount will be sent to you forthwith.

The Town Treasurer, {%t:09}
{%+:09}

column3:
Doedsbo efter hr. Jakob Blank

I nat doede hr. Jakob Blank en naturlig doed i sit hus i {%t:09}. Han efterlader ingen efterkommere, og hans nyligt aendrede testamente udpeger {%R:00} Leopold Jantzen som eneste arving. Gennemgangen af boet viser, at Jakob Blank, som endte sine dage i fattigdom, ejede et gaeldsbrev paa 500.000\C.
Hele beloebet vil blive sendt til jer uden ophold.

Kaemneren i {%t:09}
{%+:09}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Last time we came ashore in {%t:07}, the crew was sitting in the inn as usual when some drunken sailor started bellowing stories about the Kobold around the room. He talked about his last ship, which was taken by the Kobold, and how he was the only person that managed to escape. You know, I don't set much store by these myths, but your crew has been on tenterhooks ever since. I have the situation under control and simply wanted to let you know.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Sidst vi gik i land i {%t:07}, sad besaetningen som saedvanlig paa kroen, da en fuld soemand begyndte at broele historier om skibsnissen ud i lokalet. Han fortalte om sit seneste skib, som skibsnissen havde taget, og om hvordan han var den eneste, der slap vaek. I ved, at jeg ikke giver meget for den slags myter, men jeres besaetning har siddet som paa naale lige siden. Jeg har situationen under kontrol og ville blot lade jer vide det.

Styrmanden paa {%s:04}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Strange sightings have been reported near {%t:07}. Several sailors have claimed on separate occasions that they have seen a ghost ship gliding through the waves under full sail, even though there was no wind. When they heard this, the crew's hearts sank, but they bravely continued with their duties. I have assigned twice as many guards as usual in an attempt to stop them worrying.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Der er meldt om maerkelige syn naer {%t:07}. Flere soemaend har ved forskellige lejligheder paastaaet, at de har set et spoegelsesskib glide over boelgerne for fulde sejl, skoent der ikke var vind. Da besaetningen hoerte det, sank modet, men de fortsatte tappert med deres arbejde. Jeg har sat dobbelt saa mange vagter som ellers for at proeve at berolige dem.

Styrmanden paa {%s:04}

column2:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

The cowardly rabble has fled. While we have been here in {%t:08}, every sailor except me has jumped ship for fear of the Kobold. You will have to enlist a new crew before we can set sail again, whether you want to or not.

Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03}{%N:0A},

Det feje pak er flygtet. Mens vi laa her i {%t:08}, er hver eneste soemand undtagen mig deserteret af frygt for skibsnissen. Hvad enten I vil eller ej, maa I hyre en ny besaetning, foer vi kan saette sejl igen.

Styrmanden paa {%s:04}

column2:
Most esteemed {%R:01} {%n:01},

As we can see from Rostock, you certainly don't stint on your deeds. So we hope you will accept another sum by way of thanks, which you can invest in the town's further improvement right away. This time it is {%c:00}.

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Hoejt aerede {%R:01} {%n:01},

Som vi kan se i Rostock, sparer I sandelig ikke paa jeres gerninger. Derfor haaber vi, at I vil tage imod endnu et beloeb som tak, som I straks kan investere i byens videre opsving. Denne gang drejer det sig om {%c:00}.

Oldermanden {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
Worthy {%R:01} {%n:01},

You have not betrayed our confidence in you at all - on the contrary: Stettin is positively flourishing. So please take these {%c:00} for your future projects. This gold was donated by wealthy former traders to the Hanseatic League to be used for whatever purpose you wish.

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Vaerdige {%R:01} {%n:01},

I har ikke svigtet vores tillid, tvaertimod: Stettin blomstrer for alvor. Tag derfor imod disse {%c:00} til jeres fremtidige projekter. Dette guld er skaenket Hansaen af rige tidligere handelsmaend til at bruge til ethvert formaal, I oensker.

Oldermanden {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
Welcome, {%R:01} {%n:01},

Stockholm has once again become a magnificent town and we have you to thank for this. Take these {%c:00} as a token of our appreciation.

Your Alderman {%F:00}{%+:03}

column3:
Velkommen, {%R:01} {%n:01},

Stockholm er igen blevet en praegtig by, og det har vi jer at takke for. Tag imod disse {%c:00} som tegn paa vores paaskoennelse.

Jeres oldermand {%F:00}{%+:03}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

So I've been waiting and waiting and still no sign of my daughter? I was certainly wrong about you. Fine, I'll try and find her myself. I still have some hope.

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Jeg venter og venter, og stadig intet spor af min datter? Jeg tog sandelig fejl af jer. Godt, saa proever jeg selv at finde hende. Jeg har endnu lidt haab.

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

This is the end for me! The last pleasure in my life has been sunk with that pirate {%N:06}'s cog! How could you have let that happen? May this deed be an onerous burden on your conscience forever!

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Dette er min undergang! Den sidste glaede i mit liv er sunket med piraten {%N:06}s kogge! Hvordan kunne I lade det ske? Maa denne gerning for altid tynge jeres samvittighed!

{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}

column2:
To all long distance traders!

Arsonists have turned our town into a flaming inferno, and we are very short of raw materials for rebuilding it. In order to increase our supplies of iron goods and bricks, previously stored fur stocks are being offered at reasonable prices in the market square.

Mayor of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Til alle fjernhandlere!

Brandstiftere har forvandlet vores by til et flammehav, og vi mangler haardt raavarer til genopbygningen. For at oege vores beholdninger af isenkram og mursten udbydes oplagrede pelsbeholdninger til rimelige priser paa torvet.

Borgmesteren i {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
{%R:01} {%n:01},

I need your help! The wells in my town have been contaminated and now there is a plague raging relentlessly through the streets. I know you've already done a lot for my friends and me, but I beg you just to keep an eye on things, so that my lovely town is still well provided for.

Mayor of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
{%R:01} {%n:01},

Jeg har brug for jeres hjaelp! Broendene i min by er blevet forurenet, og nu raser pesten ubarmhjertigt gennem gaderne. Jeg ved, at I allerede har gjort meget for mine venner og mig, men jeg beder jer blot holde oeje med tingene, saa min smukke by fortsat er godt forsynet.

Borgmesteren i {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Dear {%R:01} {%n:01},
The upturn of the Hanseatic League is complete! How can we ever thank you enough? You have saved the Hanseatic League and given new powers to the community. The townspeople will never forget you!

The Alderman {%F:00}{%+:0D}

column3:
Kaere {%R:01} {%n:01},
Hansaens opsving er fuldbragt! Hvordan kan vi nogensinde takke jer nok? I har reddet Hansaen og givet faellesskabet nye kraefter. Borgerne vil aldrig glemme jer!

Oldermanden {%F:00}{%+:0D}

column2:
Dear {%R:06} {%n:06},

Not very long ago, a terrible plague afflicted our town. Could you help us to rebuild London again? You will receive a handsome sum as payment if London can attract 1,000 new permanent residents and be restored to its former splendour.

The Mayor of London{%+:01}

column3:
Kaere {%R:06} {%n:06},

For ikke saa laenge siden ramte en frygtelig pest vores by. Kunne I hjaelpe os med at genopbygge London? I faar en paen sum i betaling, hvis London kan tiltraekke 1.000 nye faste indbyggere og genvinde sin tidligere pragt.

Borgmesteren i London{%+:01}

column2:
Dear {%R:06} {%n:06},

Thank you for helping us to rebuild London again. By way of thanks, I have had several deliveries of surplus wool brought to your trading office in Rostock.

The Mayor of London{%+:01}

column3:
Kaere {%R:06} {%n:06},

Tak fordi I hjalp os med at genopbygge London. Som tak har jeg ladet flere leverancer overskydende uld bringe til jeres kontor i Rostock.

Borgmesteren i London{%+:01}

column2:
Our saviour, {%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

What a wonderful blessing - you have liberated Stettin from the evil pirate. Now the long distance traders can put in at our town again without fear. Be assured of our eternal gratitude. We cannot give you gold, but we will reward you by filling your trading office with barrels of beer.

Mayor of Stettin{%+:03}

column3:
Vor redningsmand, {%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Hvilken vidunderlig velsignelse: I har befriet Stettin for den onde pirat. Nu kan fjernhandlerne igen anloebe vores by uden frygt. Vaer forvisset om vores evige taknemmelighed. Guld kan vi ikke give jer, men vi beloenner jer ved at fylde jeres kontor med toender oel.

Borgmesteren i Stettin{%+:03}

column2:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

The pirate outside Stettin has not been seen again and only the Kobold himself knows what could have happened. But that isn't our problem, and we are hoping with all our hearts that the pirate will stay missing.

Mayor of Stettin{%+:03}

column3:
{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02},

Piraten ud for Stettin er ikke set igen, og kun skibsnissen selv ved, hvad der kan vaere sket. Men det er ikke vores problem, og vi haaber af hele vores hjerte, at piraten forbliver forsvundet.

Borgmesteren i Stettin{%+:03}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

It has come to our attention that some of the Dutch King's saboteurs have settled in {%t:01}. They probably want to prevent the Hanseatic League regaining its former position of power. Keep an eye on your stocks of goods! As soon as we know where these miscreants are lurking, we will contact you again.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Kaere {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Det er kommet os for oere, at nogle af den hollandske konges sabotoerer har slaaet sig ned i {%t:01}. De vil formentlig forhindre Hansaen i at genvinde sin tidligere magtposition. Hold oeje med jeres varelagre! Saa snart vi ved, hvor disse skurke holder til, kontakter vi jer igen.

Hansaens raad{%+:05}

column2:
To all traders from Rostock,

An underhand act of sabotage destroyed all of the town's grain stocks as well as those belonging to some traders today. A search for the culprits is currently underway.

The Mayor{%+:01}

column3:
Til alle handelsmaend fra Rostock,

En lumsk sabotage oedelagde i dag alle byens kornlagre samt nogle handelsmaends. Man leder i oejeblikket efter gerningsmaendene.

Borgmesteren{%+:01}

column2:
To all traders from Rostock,

The saboteurs have struck again.

The Mayor{%+:01}

column3:
Til alle handelsmaend fra Rostock,

Sabotoererne har slaaet til igen.

Borgmesteren{%+:01}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Our suspicions were right. It seems that the mayor of Bruges was coerced into the wicked acts by a councillor called {%N:0A} with forged documents. The councillor himself was commissioned by the Dutch King to worm his way into the mayor's confidence, with a view to weakening the Hanseatic League through piracy and sabotage. As far as we can tell, the mayor of Bruges is not to blame at all, however the corrupt {%N:0A} has escaped.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Kaere {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Vores mistanke var rigtig. Det ser ud til, at borgmesteren i Bruges blev tvunget til de onde gerninger med forfalskede dokumenter af en raadsherre ved navn {%N:0A}. Raadsherren havde selv faaet til opgave af den hollandske konge at indynde sig hos borgmesteren for at svaekke Hansaen med soeroeveri og sabotage. Saa vidt vi kan se, er borgmesteren i Bruges slet ikke skyld i noget, men den korrupte {%N:0A} er undsluppet.

Hansaens raad{%+:05}

column2:
Dear {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Thank goodness! It is over! {%N:0A}, the wicked Dutchman, has finally been destroyed! Now the oceans and towns are safer places again and nothing else can stand in the way of the Hanseatic League's growth.

The Hanseatic League council{%+:05}

column3:
Kaere {%R:00} {%v:00} {%n:00},

Gudskelov! Det er forbi! {%N:0A}, den onde hollaender, er endelig tilintetgjort! Nu er havene og byerne igen mere sikre, og intet staar laengere i vejen for Hansaens vaekst.

Hansaens raad{%+:05}

column2:
{%7:03},

Last time we came ashore in {%t:07}, the crew was sitting in the inn as usual when some drunken sailor started bellowing stories about the Kobold around the room. He talked about his last ship, which was taken by the Kobold, and how he was the only person that managed to escape. You know, I don't set much store by these myths, but your crew has been on tenterhooks ever since. I have the situation under control and simply wanted to let you know.

