Helmsman of the {%s:04}

column3:
{%7:03},

Det feje pak er flygtet. Mens vi laa her i {%t:08}, er hver eneste soemand undtagen mig deserteret af frygt for skibsnissen. Hvad enten I vil eller ej, maa I hyre en ny besaetning, foer vi kan saette sejl igen.

Styrmanden paa {%s:04}

column2:
Greetings,

The problems that we assigned you to deal with have been resolved. Our friends have urged us to settle the conflict in a peaceful, civilised manner.

{%N:09}

column3:
Vaer hilset,

De problemer, vi bad jer tage jer af, er loest. Vores venner har tilskyndet os til at bilaegge konflikten paa en fredelig og civiliseret maade.

{%N:09}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Your ship, {%s:05}, is riddled with barnacles. This means that the condition of your ship is much worse than previously thought.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Jeres skib {%s:05} er fuldt af rurer. Det betyder, at skibets tilstand er langt vaerre end antaget.

Havnefogeden i {%t:07}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

It has come to our attention that the planks on your ship, {%s:05}, are in a much worse condition than previously thought. You are therefore strongly advised to have your ship repaired.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Vi har konstateret, at plankerne paa jeres skib {%s:05} er i langt daarligere stand end antaget. Vi raader jer derfor indtraengende til at faa skibet repareret.

Havnefogeden i {%t:07}

column2:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

It has been ascertained that the damage to your ship, {%s:05}, is much more serious than previously thought. It is in your own interests that we advise you to have the ship repaired as soon as possible.

Harbour-master of {%t:07}

column3:
{%7:01}{%N:08},

Det er blevet fastslaaet, at skaderne paa jeres skib {%s:05} er langt alvorligere end antaget. I jeres egen interesse raader vi jer til at faa skibet repareret snarest muligt.

Havnefogeden i {%t:07}

column2:
The pirate has been killed, but not by one of your ships!
So you are hardly entitled to the reward I promised you.

{%V:08} {%N:07}

column3:
Piraten er draebt, men ikke af et af jeres skibe!
Saa I har naeppe krav paa den beloenning, jeg lovede jer.

{%V:08} {%N:07}

column2:
Hear ye! Oh Hear ye, citizens!

Tidings of our peaceful town's success have spread far beyond the city limits. Now despicable evil forces are plotting against our interests, demanding that we hand over the merchandise that we have worked so hard to produce. It is coming to our attention that a huge army of mercenaries will soon be coming to inundate us with murder, fire and looting.
We need to take precautions quickly to protect our homes, for we suspect there will be no way of averting this bloodthirsty assault.

The town of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Hoer, hoer, borgere!

Rygtet om vores fredelige bys fremgang har spredt sig langt ud over bygraensen. Nu smeder foragtelige onde magter raenker mod vores interesser og kraever, at vi udleverer de varer, vi saa moejsommeligt har fremstillet. Det er kommet os for oere, at en vaeldig haer af lejesoldater snart vil oversvoemme os med mord, brand og plyndring.
Vi maa hurtigt traeffe forholdsregler for at beskytte vores hjem, for vi frygter, at dette blodtoerstige angreb ikke kan afvaerges.

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Citizens of {%t:04}!

Hordes of marauding mercenaries are sweeping through the land, leaving murder and pillage in their wake. No atrocity is beyond them. Who knows whether our prayers will be answered, so that they may leave our beautiful town alone?
So prepare yourselves, fortify the walls and stand by your arms.
May the walls and our courage hold!

The town of {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column3:
Borgere i {%t:04}!

Horder af plyndrende lejesoldater drager gennem landet og efterlader mord og plyndring. Ingen grusomhed er dem fremmed. Hvem ved, om vores boenner bliver hoert, saa de lader vores smukke by i fred?
Goer jer derfor rede, befaest murene og hold vaabnene parat.
Maa murene og vores mod holde!

Byen {%t:04}
{%+:04}

column2:
Our gruelling business in {%t:08} is now complete.
I trust this has not tried your patience too much, and I would be grateful if you would now take me to {%t:00}.

Courier on board the {%s:05}

column3:
Vores opslidende forretninger i {%t:08} er nu afsluttet.
Jeg haaber ikke, at det har sat jeres taalmodighed alt for meget paa proeve, og jeg ville vaere taknemmelig, hvis I nu foerte mig til {%t:00}.

Kureren om bord paa {%s:05}

column2:
Dear Sir or Madam,

The Hanseatic League is delighted to announce that a race will be taking place on {%D:01} between the Hanseatic League's boldest traders!
The voyage begins in {%t:15} and takes the participants to {%t:18}. Curious onlookers are more than welcome to attend the race.
The following traders are taking part in the race:

{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02}
{%R:03} {%v:03} {%n:03}
{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}
{%R:05} {%v:05} {%n:05}
{%R:06} {%v:06} {%n:06}
{%R:07} {%v:07} {%n:07}
{%R:08} {%v:08} {%n:08}
{%R:09} {%v:09} {%n:09}

The wagers have been collected from all participating Traders. They must arrive on the {%t:15} with their competing ships. 
The fastest ships will then run the race at dawn on the {%D:01}. 

May the fastest ship win!

The Court of the Hanse!

{%+:12}

column3:
Kaere herre eller frue,

Hansaen har fornoejelsen at meddele, at der den {%D:01} afholdes en kapsejlads mellem Hansaens dristigste handelsmaend!
Rejsen begynder i {%t:15} og foerer deltagerne til {%t:18}. Nysgerrige tilskuere er mere end velkomne.
Foelgende handelsmaend deltager i kapsejladsen:

{%R:02} {%v:02} {%n:02}
{%R:03} {%v:03} {%n:03}
{%R:04} {%v:04} {%n:04}
{%R:05} {%v:05} {%n:05}
{%R:06} {%v:06} {%n:06}
{%R:07} {%v:07} {%n:07}
{%R:08} {%v:08} {%n:08}
{%R:09} {%v:09} {%n:09}

Indsatserne er opkraevet hos alle deltagende handelsmaend. De skal moede op i {%t:15} med deres kapsejladsskibe.
De hurtigste skibe sejler saa kapsejladsen ved daggry den {%D:01}.

Maa det hurtigste skib vinde!

Hansaens domstol!

{%+:12}

